Presidential elections were held in [[East Timor]] on 20 March 2017. Incumbent President [[Taur Matan Ruak]], who was eligible for a second term, chose not to run for re-election.<ref name=ST>[http://www.straitstimes.com/asia/se-asia/east-timor-to-hold-presidential-poll-in-march East Timor to hold presidential poll in March] Straits Times, 18 January 2017</ref> The result was a victory for [[Francisco Guterres]] of [[Revolutionary Front for an Independent East Timor|FRETILIN]].<ref>[https://expresso.sapo.pt/internacional/2017-03-21-Francisco-Guterres-Lu-Olo-eleito-Presidente-de-Timor-Leste Francisco Guterres Lu-Olo eleito Presidente de Timor-Leste] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181118205757/https://expresso.sapo.pt/internacional/2017-03-21-Francisco-Guterres-Lu-Olo-eleito-Presidente-de-Timor-Leste |date=2018-11-18 }} Expresso, 21 March 2017</ref>

==Electoral system==
The [[President of East Timor]] is elected using the [[two-round system]].<ref>[http://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/2231/ Democratic Republic of Timor-Leste] IFES</ref> If it had been required, a second round would have been held on 20 April.<ref name=ST/>

